{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/940247-wip-abyssals-honour-bound-to-desolation","id":940247,"title":"WIP Abyssals: Honour-bound to Desolation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-30T14:07:23-07:00","id":940247,"title":"WIP Abyssals: Honour-bound to Desolation","content":"This is a bit of my own attempt at a fan splat for Abyssals. Right now, I'm working on setting down the foundations before going into detail, but I think the Codex Solitudo is going to be central to them, as both a social contract and a guideline to help build a new form of Resonance.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1o-rU-PZVAbG9U7ZYGN7JAMRcBG_fLYUpWC_LWk2tSO8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a> It's barely started, but I've been dealing with a really bad migraine for two days now, so... it's what I got down in a decent 20 minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:03:12-07:00","id":940280,"title":"","content":"I like it! Sounds a bit different from my feeble scrabblings (which I need to work on again) but you seem to have a solid thematic focus. Noice.<br /> <br /> Also hope that headache goes away---I have two loved ones who suffer migraines and I know they suuuuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 07-30-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:07:52-07:00","id":940435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/940247-wip-abyssals-honour-bound-to-desolation#post940247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been dealing with a really bad migraine for two days now</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered chiropractic adjustments?<br /> <br /> A crick in your neck pulls muscles painfully tense in a cascading effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T07:17:37-07:00","id":940612,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure it's not a crick in the neck. It's very much migraines. I've had them regularly since I was pretty young. Sensitivity to light, sound, and warmth. So... yeah. But thanks for the concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:10:57-07:00","id":940624,"title":"","content":"So I added a bit more, a discussion of Deathmarks and the idea of what Resonance is (I still need time to work on actual rules for Resonance). As a bit of a teaser, I see Deathmarks as something not unlike the old Lunar Tell. But unlike the Tell, it's something that you know SHOULD have killed someone, but you can tell yourself they were lucky. At least till their anima begins to show. Rather than the caste mark bleeding, the wound/scar glows (or somehow otherwise draws attention, this is a place I think the player should be able to customize as long as it WILL draw attention) and starts bleeding, stigmata style. It's still horrifying, but also should provoke a small sense of sadness, rather than looking like they're a bloodsoaked killer. They might be, but I think a player should be able to define this more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T18:37:46-07:00","id":940985,"title":"","content":"Passions (all new mechanic) and Resonance rules added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T07:41:04-07:00","id":941178,"title":"","content":"That's a really cool way to do it! All this great writing on your end has sort of pushed me to go back and start trying to work on my own thematic base.<br /> <br /> What do you plan to do with the &quot;Romance of the Grave&quot; concept mentioned in the core?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T10:25:58-07:00","id":941253,"title":"","content":"Had to look at that exactly, but I think that actually is a tough one. But that said... I look at this and I see something that sees life and death intertwined. Without life, death is meaningless. A death where the person has not even tried to live is a sad and hollow thing. But a person dying doing what they love or believe in? That is a good thing. And the Romance of the Grave section speaks to that. If death requires life to be meaningful, then life is made only the more full for death existing. Abyssals are people who came to treasure life more than any other in their dying. Maybe it's only their own life. Maybe it's life in general. But looking upon the sad beauty that reminds them of that period also makes them thankful to be alive. (which thanks... this will find a place into it definitely).<br /> <br /> Of course, like it said, Abyssals are many and varied, and there are those who feel differently. In fact, I think I'll add that right not.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also adding some possible origins","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 08-01-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T10:19:14-07:00","id":943695,"title":"","content":"I need to be off for an appointment, but I just added some stuff about optional forms of Exaltation preludes and Artfacts/Familiar origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:29:20-07:00","id":944560,"title":"","content":"Lastly, added the code of isolation (or a start). This is a purely setting thing, and each Abyssal will view them differently, but tend to know them roughly at worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"a